[2026-07-18T19:10:00Z] Starting correction pass 3 for EAI-TASK-040.

PM blocking defect (2026-07-18T17:14:29Z):
- Signal handler path (handleSignal) performs shutdown actions but never calls
  detachSignalHandlers(). Only explicit stop() path detaches listeners.
- In a host process, stale owned listeners remain attached with closed-over
  lock references.
- Required: fix handleSignal to detach listeners, add in-process test.

================================================================================
Fix 1: src/runtime-supervisor.js
================================================================================
Added detachSignalHandlers() call after releaseSupervisorLock and onShutdown
in the handleSignal function (3 lines added).

================================================================================
Fix 2: tests/runtime-supervisor.test.mjs
================================================================================
Added in-process signal handler test that:
- Creates supervisor in same process
- Counts baseline SIGTERM/SIGINT listeners
- Verifies listeners added on start
- Gets actual registered SIGTERM handler from process.listeners()
- Invokes it directly
- Verifies:
  - Listener counts returned to baseline (both SIGTERM and SIGINT)
  - Heartbeat has lastResult: "SHUTDOWN"
  - Supervisor lock is released
  - Fresh supervisor instance can start

